1. Attribution (Section 7(b))
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Works containing this material that display Appropriate Legal Notices
must include in those notices the copyright notice designated in
ATTRIBUTION.txt as published by the Warzone 2100 Project in the version
from which this material was obtained or derived.

The Warzone 2100 Project also asks that those notices include the
project website link designated in ATTRIBUTION.txt, as an active
hyperlink where they can display hyperlinks, so that users can find
the official project.

Nothing in this clause shall be construed to prohibit additional
notices otherwise permitted or required by the License, provided that
such notices do not obscure or replace the notices required above.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Origin and modified versions (Sections 7(c) and 7(d))
------------------------------------------------------------------------

(a) Origin

You may not misrepresent the origin of this material, including by:

  - representing this material, or any copy or build containing it, as
    provided, distributed, or endorsed by the Warzone 2100 Project when
    it is not; or

  - setting, copying, or altering build or version information (such
    as a distributor identifier, version-control data, or a build
    manifest) so that a build appears to have been produced or released
    by the Warzone 2100 Project when it was not.

Information that a build generates itself, from the source and data it
was actually built from or from its own outputs, is not copied or
altered for this purpose. Builds made on behalf of, or under the
direction of, the Warzone 2100 Project are produced by it for this
purpose.

Conveying the original version, or a version of it whose changes from
the original version are all of the kinds listed in clause 2(d) and
meet the conditions of that clause, under the name "Warzone 2100" and
with the notices these terms require is not by itself a
misrepresentation. Including the notices required by clause 1 is not by
itself a representation that a copy or build is provided, distributed,
or endorsed by the Warzone 2100 Project.

(b) Marking of modified versions

A modified version that you convey must be marked as different from
the original version as follows:

  (i)  It may truthfully describe itself as based on Warzone 2100, but
       it must be presented under a product name that does not include
       "Warzone 2100" or a variant spelling or abbreviation of it (such
       as "Warzone2100" or "WZ2100"). The product name is the name
       shown in the program's own interface (such as its window title
       and main menu), in application launchers and software centers,
       and in store listings and similar descriptions of it.

  (ii) Where it has an interactive user interface, it must clearly and
       legibly display a notice identifying it as an unofficial
       modified version of Warzone 2100 (for example, "Based on
       Warzone 2100 - unofficial modified version") on its main menu
       (or equivalent primary screen), or in another place at least as
       prominent. Where the original version prints a startup banner
       or version output, the corresponding output of the modified
       version must also include such a notice.

This clause does not require changing the names of executables,
application bundles, packages, files, directories, or other identifiers
by which the program is invoked, installed, or located.

(c) Scope of marking

Clause 2(b) applies to a modified version that is, or is derived from,
the Warzone 2100 game as a whole (including with material added or
removed), or that is likely to be taken for a version of it. It does
not apply to:

  - a separate program that incorporates only portions of this
    material, and is not likely to be taken for a version of the
    Warzone 2100 game;

  - mods, maps, or other add-ons; or

  - a build distributed only for testing changes proposed for inclusion
    in the original version, and clearly identified as a test build in
    its version information.

Those remain subject to clause 2(a).

Using the program's built-in mod, map, or add-on mechanisms does not by
itself create a modified version for the purposes of this clause.
However, a version distributed with mods, maps, or add-ons installed or
enabled by default, other than those of the original version or
otherwise published by the Warzone 2100 Project, is a modified version
if they modify or replace this material, and the exclusion of mods,
maps, and add-ons in this clause does not apply to it.

(d) Changes that do not create a modified version

For the purposes of this clause, a version is not a modified version if
its changes from the original version are limited to:

  (1) selecting build options provided by the original version's build
      system (for example, to disable optional integrations);

  (2) changes to building, packaging, installation, file locations, and
      packaging metadata;

  (3) changes for compatibility with, or to use, libraries, fonts, or
      other components of the host system;

  (4) launchers or wrappers whose only function is to start the program
      and configure its execution environment, such as sandboxing;

  (5) fixes for security vulnerabilities, provided that they do not
      remove or disable features of the original version beyond what
      is reasonably necessary to fix the vulnerability;

  (6) fixes for defects that correspond to fixes made in the original
      version, including adaptations of those fixes to earlier
      releases; and

  (7) translations taken from the original version's translation
      sources;

provided that, apart from the direct effects of those changes, the
version's gameplay, features, content, and behavior are those of the
original version; that the changes do not remove or disable features
or content of the original version, except by selecting options under
item (1) or as permitted by item (5); that they do not cause it to
collect or transmit data it otherwise would not, or to display
advertising; and that they do not alter or obscure the notices required
by these terms.

